L 34.671875 8.6875 \nQ 35.640625 5.375 37.3125 5.375 \nQ 38.765625 5.375 40.421875 6.890625 \nQ 42.09375 8.40625 42.78125 9.671875 \nQ 43.171875 9.671875 43.75 8.890625 \nQ 44.34375 8.109375 44.34375 7.71875 \nQ 44.046875 6.0625 40.71875 2.78125 \nQ 37.40625 -0.484375 34.375 -0.484375 \nQ 30.28125 -0.484375 27.734375 8.015625 \nL 25.484375 15.625 \nL 19.34375 4.984375 \nQ 16.109375 -0.59375 11.140625 -0.59375 \nQ 7.8125 -0.59375 5.46875 1.375 \nQ 4.6875 2.734375 4.6875 3.90625 \nQ 4.6875 5.375 5.703125 6.390625 \nQ 6.734375 7.421875 7.8125 7.421875 \nQ 9.078125 7.421875 10.6875 5.90625 \nQ 12.3125 4.390625 13.671875 4.390625 \nQ 14.84375 4.390625 16.3125 6.9375 \nL 24.03125 20.21875 \nL 20.015625 33.296875 \nQ 19.046875 36.625 17.390625 36.625 \nQ 15.921875 36.625 14.25 35.109375 \nQ 12.59375 33.59375 11.921875 32.328125 \nQ 11.53125 32.328125 10.9375 33.109375 \nQ 10.359375 33.890625 10.359375 34.28125 \nQ 10.640625 35.9375 13.953125 39.203125 \nQ 17.28125 42.484375 20.3125 42.484375 \nz\n\" id=\"CrimsonText-Italic-120\"></path>\n     </defs>\n     <g transform=\"translate(256.271562 244.798528)scale(0.15 -0.15)\">\n      <use xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Italic-120\"></use>\n     </g>\n    </g>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"line2d_1\">\n    <path clip-path=\"url(#p7ec86fd512)\" d=\"M 41.860197 140.390597 \nL 47.533851 134.47272 \nL 52.802244 128.66784 \nL 58.070637 122.548129 \nL 63.33903 116.096511 \nL 68.607423 109.294984 \nL 73.875815 102.124572 \nL 79.144208 94.565267 \nL 84.412601 86.595977 \nL 89.680994 78.194467 \nL 94.544126 70.035347 \nL 99.407258 61.468587 \nL 104.27039 52.47382 \nL 109.133522 43.029663 \nL 113.186132 34.800083 \nL 113.186132 34.800083 \n\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-linecap:square;stroke-width:2.3;\"></path>\n   </g>\n  </g>\n </g>\n <defs>\n  <clipPath id=\"p7ec86fd512\">\n   <rect height=\"260.82\" width=\"262.488358\" x=\"9.200821\" y=\"7.2\"></rect>\n  </clipPath>\n </defs>\n</svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for graph of a curve\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>Moving from left to right:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>The curve passes through quadrant 1.</li>\n<li>The curve trends up sharply.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>The curve passes through the following points:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>(0 comma 6)</li>\n<li>(1 comma 9.0)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The graph gives the estimated population <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>, in thousands, of a town <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> years since <math alttext=\"2003\"><mn>2003</mn>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"0 less than or equals x less than or equals 5\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>5</mn></math>. Which of the following best describes the increase in the estimated population from&nbsp;<math alttext=\"x equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> to&nbsp;<math alttext=\"x equals 1\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"8eabbb42-5eae-48b2-9034-90a716f2cc6f","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The estimated population at&nbsp;<math alttext=\"x equals 1\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> is <math alttext=\"0.5\"><mn>0.5</mn></math> times the estimated population at <math alttext=\"x equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>"},{"id":"746737e7-620e-45f4-b952-be033a195c90","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The estimated population at&nbsp;<math alttext=\"x equals 1\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> is <math alttext=\"1.5\"><mn>1.5</mn></math> times the estimated population at&nbsp;<math alttext=\"x equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>"},{"id":"dc3e7185-8e1d-4150-974c-bbb5c3abb3af","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The estimated population at&nbsp;<math alttext=\"x equals 1\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> is <math alttext=\"2.5\"><mn>2.5</mn></math> times the estimated population at <math alttext=\"x equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>"},{"id":"935641be-e02b-4815-b23f-500fe59aeea0","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The estimated population at&nbsp;<math alttext=\"x equals 1\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> is <math alttext=\"3.5\"><mn>3.5</mn></math> times the estimated population at <math alttext=\"x equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>"}],"keys":["746737e7-620e-45f4-b952-be033a195c90"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. On the graph shown, the <em>y</em>-axis represents estimated population, in thousands. The graph shows that when <math alttext=\"x equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, the <em>y</em>-coordinate is <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math>. Therefore, the estimated population at <math alttext=\"x equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> thousand. The graph also shows that when <math alttext=\"x equals 1\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, the <em>y</em>-coordinate is <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math>. Therefore, the estimated population at <math alttext=\"x equals 1\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math> thousand. Dividing <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math> thousand by <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> thousand yields <math alttext=\"1.5\"><mn>1.5</mn>\n</math>; therefore, <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math> thousand is <math alttext=\"1.5\"><mn>1.5</mn>\n</math> times <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> thousand. It follows that the estimated population at <math alttext=\"x equals 1\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"1.5\"><mn>1.5</mn>\n</math> times the estimated population at <math alttext=\"x equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect&nbsp;and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect&nbsp;and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1730147357398,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"f1fa0821","skill_cd":"P.C.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","createDate":1730147357398,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"","external_id":"8fbdc9d2-8c5f-4da3-98db-20599f2fff76","primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"b1ed6e0c-a9b1-4e76-955f-e3afa1deb952","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"answerOptions":[{"content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The estimated population at&nbsp;<math alttext=\"x equals 1\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> is <math alttext=\"0.5\"><mn>0.5</mn></math> times the estimated population at <math alttext=\"x equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>","id":"8eabbb42-5eae-48b2-9034-90a716f2cc6f"},{"content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The estimated population at&nbsp;<math alttext=\"x equals 1\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> is <math alttext=\"1.5\"><mn>1.5</mn></math> times the estimated population at&nbsp;<math alttext=\"x equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>","id":"746737e7-620e-45f4-b952-be033a195c90"},{"content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The estimated population at&nbsp;<math alttext=\"x equals 1\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> is <math alttext=\"2.5\"><mn>2.5</mn></math> times the estimated population at <math alttext=\"x equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>","id":"dc3e7185-8e1d-4150-974c-bbb5c3abb3af"},{"content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The estimated population at&nbsp;<math alttext=\"