renthesis x right parenthesis equals 1.23\"><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1.23</mn></math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"1.23\"><mn>1.23</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"h left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> in <math alttext=\"h left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals upper C a Superscript x\"><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></math> yields <math alttext=\"1.23 equals upper C a Superscript 0\"><mn>1.23</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></math>, or <math alttext=\"1.23 equals upper C\"><mn>1.23</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"1.23\"><mn>1.23</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"upper C\"><mi>C</mi>\n</math> in <math alttext=\"h left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals upper C a Superscript x\"><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></math> yields <math alttext=\"h left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 1.23 a Superscript x\"><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1.23</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></math>. It's also given that when <math alttext=\"x equals 2\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"h left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 1.54\"><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1.54</mn></math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"1.54\"><mn>1.54</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"h left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> in <math alttext=\"h left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 1.23 a Superscript x\"><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1.23</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></math> yields <math alttext=\"1.54 equals 1.23 a squared\"><mn>1.54</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1.23</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"1.23\"><mn>1.23</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"StartFraction 1.54 Over 1.23 EndFraction equals StartFraction 1.23 a squared Over 1.23 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>1.54</mn><mn>1.23</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.23</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>1.23</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext=\"a squared\"><msup>\n<mi>a</mi>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</math> is approximately equal to <math alttext=\"1.252\"><mn>1.252</mn>\n</math>. Since <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> is positive, <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> is approximately equal to <math alttext=\"StartRoot 1.252 EndRoot\"><msqrt><mn>1.252</mn></msqrt></math>, or <math alttext=\"1.12\"><mn>1.12</mn>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"1.12\"><mn>1.12</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> in <math alttext=\"h left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 1.23 a Superscript x\"><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1.23</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></math> yields <math alttext=\"h left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 1.23 left parenthesis 1.12 right parenthesis Superscript x\"><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1.23</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.12</mn></mfenced><mi>x</mi></msup></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. When <math alttext=\"x equals 0\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, the value of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"h left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> in this function is equal to <math alttext=\"1.12\"><mn>1.12</mn>\n</math> rather than <math alttext=\"1.23\"><mn>1.23</mn>\n</math>, and it is decreasing rather than increasing.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. When <math alttext=\"x equals 0\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"h left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> in this&nbsp;function is equal to <math alttext=\"1.12\"><mn>1.12</mn>\n</math> rather than <math alttext=\"1.23\"><mn>1.23</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This function is decreasing rather than increasing.</p>","externalid":"2a0b1f88-5e2b-441c-84cb-141f8592d02a","correct_answer":["D"]},"createDate":1743430554981,"updateDate":1743430554981}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430554981, 1743430554981),
    ($SATQ$f44a29a8$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$045551-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">An object&rsquo;s kinetic energy, in joules, is equal to the product of one-half the object&rsquo;s mass, in kilograms, and the square of the object&rsquo;s speed, in meters per second. What is the speed, in meters per second, of an object with a mass of 4 kilograms and kinetic energy of 18 joules?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">3</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">6</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">9</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">36</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that an object&rsquo;s kinetic energy, in joules, is equal to the product of one-half the object&rsquo;s mass, in kilograms, and the square of the object&rsquo;s speed, in meters per second. This relationship can be represented by the equation <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f44a29a8/img_000_51d7107b.png" alt="K equals, one half m v squared"></span>, where <span class="italic">K</span> is the kinetic energy, <span class="italic">m </span>is the mass, and <span class="italic">v </span>is the speed. Substituting a mass of 4 kilograms for <span class="italic">m </span>and a kinetic energy of 18 joules for <span class="italic">K </span>results in the equation <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f44a29a8/img_001_65c5a823.png" alt="18 equals, one half times 4, times v squared"></span>, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f44a29a8/img_002_50b3f22b.png" alt="18 equals, 2 v squared"></span>. Dividing both sides of this equation by 2 yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f44a29a8/img_003_dd19e84d.png" alt="9 equals, v squared"></span>. Taking the square root of both sides yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f44a29a8/img_004_ae13a61f.png" alt="v equals, negative 3"></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f44a29a8/img_005_d911c1be.png" alt="v equals 3"></span>. Since speed can&rsquo;t be expressed as a negative number, the speed of the object is 3 meters per second.<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from computation errors. Choice C is incorrect. This is the value of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f44a29a8/img_006_f3b8f3d9.png" alt="v squared  "></span> rather than <span class="italic">v</span>. Choice D is incorrect. This is the value of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f44a29a8/img_007_f488b44b.png" alt="4 v squared  "></span> rather than <span class="italic">v</span>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"f44a29a8","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"045551-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.C.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">An object&rsquo;s kinetic energy, in joules, is equal to the product of one-half the object&rsquo;s mass, in kilograms, and the square of the object&rsquo;s speed, in meters per second. What is the speed, in meters per second, of an object with a mass of 4 kilograms and kinetic energy of 18 joules?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">3</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">6</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">9</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">36</p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that an object&rsquo;s kinetic energy, in joules, is equal to the product of one-half the object&rsquo;s mass, in kilograms, and the square of the object&rsquo;s speed, in meters per second. This relationship can be represented by the equation <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f44a29a8/img_000_51d7107b.png\" alt=\"K equals, one half m v squared\"></span>, where <span class=\"italic\">K</span> is the kinetic energy, <span class=\"italic\">m </span>is the mass, and <span class=\"italic\">v </span>is the speed. Substituting a mass of 4 kilograms for <span class=\"italic\">m </span>and a kinetic energy of 18 joules for <span class=\"italic\">K </span>results in the equation <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f44a29a8/img_001_65c5a823.png\" alt=\"18 equals, one half times 4, times v squared\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f44a29a8/img_002_50b3f22b.png\" alt=\"18 equals, 2 v squared\"></span>. Dividing both sides of this equation by 2 yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f44a29a8/img_003_dd19e84d.png\" alt=\"9 equals, v squared\"></span>. Taking the square root of both sides yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f44a29a8/img_004_ae13a61f.png\" alt=\"v equals, negative 3\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f44a29a8/img_005_d911c1be.png\" alt=\"v equals 3\"></span>. Since speed can&rsquo;t be expressed as a negative number, the speed of the object is 3 meters per second.<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from computation errors. Choice C is incorrect. This is the value of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f44a29a8/img_006_f3b8f3d9.png\" alt=\"v squared  \"></span> rather than <span class=\"italic\">v</span>. Choice D is incorrect. This is the value of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f44a29a8/img_007_f488b44b.png\" alt=\"4 v squared  \"></span> rather than <span class=\"italic\">v</span>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":8,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959628,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"f44a29a8","skill_cd":"P.C.","score_band_range_cd":5,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","createDate":1691007959628,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"045551-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"740f91c1-5ba3-49c0-9df1-3b97689fa2cd","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"045551-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">An object&rsquo;s kinetic energy, in joules, is equal to the product of one-half the object&rsquo;s mass, in kilograms, and the square of the object&rsquo;s speed, in meters per second. What is the speed, in meters per second, of an object with a mass of 4 kilograms and kinetic energy of 18 joules?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">3</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">6</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">9</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">36</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"a","rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that an object&rsquo;s kinetic energy, in joules, is equal to the product of one-half the object&rsquo;s mass, in kilograms, and the square of the object&rsquo;s speed, in meters per second. This relationship can be represented by the equation <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"K equals, one half m v squared\"></span>, where <span class=\"italic\">K</span> is the kinetic energy, <span class=\"italic\">m </span>is the mass, and <span class=\"italic\">v </span>is the speed. Substituting a mass of 4 kilograms for <span class=\"italic\">m </span>and a kinetic energy of 18 joules for <span class=\"italic\">K </span>results in the equation <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"18 equals, one half times 4, times v squared\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"18 equals, 2 v squared\"></span>. Dividing both sides of this equation by 2 yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"9 equals, v squared\"></span>. Taking the square root of both sides yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"v equals, negative 3\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"v equals 3\"></span>. Since speed can&rsquo;t be expressed as a negative number, the speed of the object is 3 meters per second.<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from computation errors. Choice C is incorrect. This is the value of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"v squared  \"></span> rather than <span class=\"italic\">v</span>. Choice D is incorrect. This is the value of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"4 v squared  \"></span> rather than <span class=\"italic\">v</span>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959628,"updateDate":1691007959628}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959628, 1691007959628),
    ($SATQ$f44b4125$SATQ$, $SATQ$24e16e9f-c530-4992-98b0-9848ddf76fbb$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The functions <math alttext="f"><mi>f</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="g"><mi>g</mi>
</math> are defined by the given equations, where <math alttext="x greater than or equals 0"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Which of the following equations displays, as a constant or coefficient, the maximum value of the function it defines, where <math alttext="x greater than or equals 0"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>?</p>
<ol style="list-style-type: upper-roman;">
<li><math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 18 left parenthesis 1.25 right parenthesis Superscript x Baseline plus 41"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1.25</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>41</mn></math></li>
<li><math alttext="g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 9 left parenthesis 0.73 right parenthesis Superscript x"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>0.73</mn></mfenced><mi>x</mi></msup></math></li>
</ol>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"4308439d-5d77-4c3c-bb75-1cacc8b3576b","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span data-ssml-say-as=\"characters\">I</span> only</p>"},{"id":"d9e03237-38f7-425d-a699-82bdfadf904d","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span data-ssml-say-as=\"characters\">II</span> only</p>"},{"id":"71e41b42-a25b-4a0f-bbdb-3a10d5ba813e","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span data-ssml-say-as=\"characters\">I</span> and <span data-ssml-say-as=\"characters\">II</span></p>"},{"id":"0b86d0f0-3f18-46f5-9172-754eeb268c18","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Neither <span data-ssml-say-as=\"characters\">I</span> nor <span data-ssml-say-as=\"characters\">II</span></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["d9e03237-38f7-425d-a699-82bdfadf904d"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. For the function <math alttext="f"><mi>f</mi>
</math>, since the base of the exponent, <math alttext="1.25"><mn>1.25</mn>
</math>, is greater than <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>, the value of&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis 1.25 right parenthesis Superscript x"><msup><mfenced><mn>1.25</mn></mfenced><mi>x</mi></msup></math> increases as <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> increases. Therefore, the value of <math alttext="18 left parenthesis 1.25 right parenthesis Superscript x"><mn>18</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.25</mn></mfenced><mi>x</mi></msup></math> and the value of <math alttext="18 left parenthesis 1.25 right parenthesis Superscript x plus 41"><mn>18</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.25</mn></mfenced><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>41</mn></math> also increase as <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> increases. Since <math alttext="f"><mi>f</mi>
</math> is therefore an increasing function where <math alttext="x greater than or equals 0"><mi>x</mi><mo>&ge;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, the function <math alttext="f"><mi>f</mi>
</math> has no maximum value. For the function <math alttext="g"><mi>g</mi>
</math>, since the base of the exponent, <math alttext="0.73"><mn>0.73</mn>
</math>, is less than <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>, the value of <math alttext="left parenthesis 0.73 right parenthesis Superscript x"><msup><mfenced><mn>0.73</mn></mfenced><mi>x</mi></msup></math> decreases as <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> increases. Therefore, the value of <math alttext="9 left parenthesis 0.73 right parenthesis Superscript x"><mn>9</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>0.73</mn></mfenced><mi>x</mi></msup></math> also decreases as <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> increases. It follows that the maximum value of <math alttext="g left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> for <math alttext="x greater than or equals 0"><mi>x</mi><mo>&ge;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> occurs when <math alttext="x equals 0"><mrow>
<mi>x</mi>
<mo>=</mo>
<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Substituting <math alttext="0"><mn>0</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> in the function <math alttext="g"><mi>g</mi>
</math> yields <math alttext="g left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis equals 9 left parenthesis 0.73 right parenthesis Superscript 0"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>0.73</mn></mfenced><mn>0</mn></msup></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext="g left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis equals 9 left parenthesis 1 right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext="g left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis equals 9"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math>. Therefore, the maximum value of&nbsp;<math alttext="g left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> for&nbsp;<math alttext="x greater than or equals 0"><mi>x</mi><mo>&ge;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> is <math alttext="9"><mn>9</mn>
</math>, which appears as a coefficient in equation II. So, of the two equations given, only II displays, as a constant or coefficient, the maximum value of the function it defines, where <math alttext="x greater than or equals 0"><mi>x</mi><mo>&ge;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"f44b4125","external_id":"24e16e9f-c530-4992-98b0-9848ddf76fbb","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"d39addcb-64d5-4c48-bb5c-c8c8635e6bda","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.C.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The functions <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"g\"><mi>g</mi>\n</math> are defined by the given equations, where <math alttext=\"x greater than or equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Which of the following equations displays, as a constant or coefficient, the maximum value of the function it defines, where <math alttext=\"x greater than or equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>?</p>\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-roman;\">\n<li><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 18 left parenthesis 1.25 right parenthesis Superscript x Baseline plus 41\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1.25</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>41</mn></math></li>\n<li><math alttext=\"g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 9 left parenthesis 0.73 right parenthesis Superscript x\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>0.73</mn></mfenced><mi>x</mi></msup></math></li>\n</ol>","answerOptions":[{"id":"4308439d-5d77-4c3c-bb75-1cacc8b3576b","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span data-ssml-say-as=\"characters\">I</span> only</p>"},{"id":"d9e03237-38f7-425d-a699-82bdfadf904d","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span data-ssml-say-as=\"characters\">II</span> only</p>"},{"id":"71e41b42-a25b-4a0f-bbdb-3a10d5ba813e","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span data-ssml-say-as=\"characters\">I</span> and <span data-ssml-say-as=\"characters\">II</span></p>"},{"id":"0b86d0f0-3f18-46f5-9172-754eeb268c18","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Neither <span data-ssml-say-as=\"characters\">I</span> nor <span data-ssml-say-as=\"characters\">II</span></p>"}],"keys":["d9e03237-38f7-425d-a699-82bdfadf904d"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. For the function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math>, since the base of the exponent, <math alttext=\"1.25\"><mn>1.25</mn>\n</math>, is greater than <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>, the value of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis 1.25 right parenthesis Superscript x\"><msup><mfenced><mn>1.25</mn></mfenced><mi>x</mi></msup></math> increases as <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> increases. Therefore, the value of <math alttext=\"18 left parenthesis 1.25 right parenthesis Superscript x\"><mn>18</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.25</mn></mfenced><mi>x</mi></msup></math> and the value of <math alttext=\"18 left parenthesis 1.25 right parenthesis Superscript x plus 41\"><mn>18</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.25</mn></mfenced><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>41</mn></math> also increase as <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> increases. Since <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> is therefore an increasing function where <math alttext=\"x greater than or equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&ge;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, the function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> has no maximum value. For the function <math alttext=\"g\"><mi>g</mi>\n</math>, since the base of the exponent, <math alttext=\"0.73\"><mn>0.73</mn>\n</math>, is less than <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0.73 right parenthesis Superscript x\"><msup><mfenced><mn>0.73</mn></mfenced><mi>x</mi></msup></math> decreases as <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> increases. Therefore, the value of <math alttext=\"9 left parenthesis 0.73 right parenthesis Superscript x\"><mn>9</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>0.73</mn></mfenced><mi>x</mi></msup></math> also decreases as <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> increases. It follows that the maximum value of <math alttext=\"g left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> for <math alttext=\"x greater than or equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&ge;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> occurs when <math alttext=\"x equals 0\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> in the function <math alttext=\"g\"><mi>g</mi>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"g left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis equals 9 left parenthesis 0.73 right parenthesis Superscript 0\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>0.73</mn></mfenced><mn>0</mn></msup></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext=\"g left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis equals 9 left parenthesis 1 right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext=\"g left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis equals 9\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math>. Therefore, the maximum value of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"g left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> for&nbsp;<math alttext=\"x greater than or equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&ge;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> is <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math>, which appears as a coefficient in equation II. So, of the two equations given, only II displays, as a constant or coefficient, the maximum value of the function it defines, where <math alttext=\"x greater than or equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&ge;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1743430554980,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"f44b4125","skill_cd":"P.C.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","createDate":1743430554980,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"","external_id":"24e16e9f-c530-4992-98b0-9848ddf76fbb","primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"d39addcb-64d5-4c48-bb5c-c8c8635e6bda","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The functions <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"g\"><mi>g</mi>\n</math> are defined by the given equations, where <math alttext=\"x greater than or equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Which of the following equations displays, as a constant or coefficient, the maximum value of the function it defines, where <math alttext=\"x greater than or equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>?</p>\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-roman;\">\n<li><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 18 left parenthesis 1.25 right parenthesis Superscript x Baseline plus 41\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1.25</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>41</mn></math></li>\n<li><math alttext=\"g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 9 left parenthesis 0.73 right parenthesis Superscript x\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>0.73</mn></mfenced><mi>x</mi></msup></math></li>\n</ol>","keys":["d9e03237-38f7-425d-a699-82bdfadf904d"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"4308439d-5d77-4c