olrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f65288e8/img_008_50c66f9d.png" alt="1 equals, 4 times, open parenthesis, x plus 5, close parenthesis, squared"></span>. Dividing both sides of this equation by 4 yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f65288e8/img_009_4453f41b.png" alt="one fourth equals, open parenthesis, x plus 5, close parenthesis, squared"></span>. Taking the square root of both sides of this equation yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f65288e8/img_010_86a9ae26.png" alt="one half equals, x plus 5 "></span> or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f65288e8/img_011_cd144151.png" alt="negative one half equals, x plus 5"></span>. Therefore, a possible value of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f65288e8/img_012_08bec0fb.png" alt="x plus 5 "></span> is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f65288e8/img_013_6b62f681.png" alt="one half"></span>.<br>Choices B, C, and D are incorrect and may result from computational or conceptual errors.</p>
